Getting married at a château is one of those choices that sets the tone for a whole day. The setting is not a backdrop for photos: it is a park, stone, a light that changes the mood of a ceremony. At the Château de la Huberdière, in Touraine, we host weddings of 30 to 150 guests, on a fourteen-hectare estate given over to you alone.

Here is how we see the planning of a château wedding, and what it changes in practice for the couple.

## Why get married in a château

A château for a wedding is not only a fine address. It is a place you take over entirely, that you live over two days, where the party can run on without neighbours or an imposed curfew.

At La Huberdière, you have the château and its enclosed grounds to yourselves. No other wedding, no other group the same day. A civil ceremony under the trees, drinks on the terrace, dinner in the drawing rooms or under a marquee in the park: the space follows your programme, not the other way round. The details of exclusive use, capacity and services are on the [wedding](/en/chateau-wedding-loire) page.

## A château wedding 2 hrs 20 from Paris

Touraine has a rare advantage for a wedding: it is beautiful and it is close. Nazelles-Négron, where the château stands, is 2 hrs 20 from Paris and a little over an hour by train to Tours or Saint-Pierre-des-Corps.

That matters when you are welcoming guests from the Paris region or further afield. You marry in a Loire Valley setting without forcing an expedition on your loved ones. Guests arrive on the Friday, enjoy the Saturday and leave on the Sunday, with no road weariness.

## The spaces for the ceremony and the reception

A wedding unfolds in several acts, and each deserves its setting. The estate offers several, to combine with your programme and the weather.

- The age-old park for a civil ceremony under the centuries-old trees
- The terrace for drinks at sunset
- The great vaulted hall and the drawing rooms for dinner
- The Orangery or a marquee in the park for the dance floor
- The pool and the paths for the next day's photos

When the weather turns fickle, the indoor spaces take over without breaking the day's momentum. Nothing is left to chance: we always prepare a plan for fine weather and a fallback plan.

## How many guests, what budget

The couple's first question is almost always about capacity. The château seats up to 150 people for the meal, and the layout adapts to more intimate formats, from around thirty guests.

The budget for a château wedding depends on the season, the number of guests and the services. As a guide, exclusive use of the whole estate for a weekend, from Friday to Sunday, including the 21 beds, ranges from 4,000 € to 8,000 € depending on the season. The reception tables and chairs are available for a supplement. Rather than a fixed rate, we build a bespoke proposal once we understand your plans, with no hidden costs.

One detail couples appreciate: we charge no corkage. You bring your own wines, champagnes and spirits, and you keep control of this often heavy line of the budget.

## Housing your loved ones on site

One of the real luxuries of a château wedding is being able to house close family on site. The estate's ten suites, with their 21 beds, keep the couple and their loved ones at the heart of the celebration, with no late-night drive. You gather at dawn around coffee, you carry on the party without watching for the last taxi.

For larger guest lists, we keep a list of partner cottages and hotels less than ten minutes away. The same private-estate logic also serves [family gatherings](/en/chateau-hire-large-group) and large tables. The place is made for bringing people together.

## Suppliers, caterer and coordination

A successful wedding rests on a good team. We work with trusted suppliers from the region, caterers, florists, musicians, and we put you in touch according to the spirit you are after. You remain free to bring your own suppliers if you prefer.

A single point of contact follows you from the first meeting to the day after the party. Lodovica brings the warmth of her Italian roots, I look after the logistics. This continuity avoids nasty surprises and lets you enjoy your day.

## Getting married in any season

We often picture a wedding in summer, but the château lends itself to every season. Spring offers a park in bloom, autumn its warm colours, winter the intimacy of the drawing rooms and the log fire. Each season has its light and its mood, and marrying outside the busiest months also leaves more choice of dates.

## Planning your château wedding

A fine wedding is prepared without haste. We guide every couple on the choice of date, the running of the two days and the coordination with suppliers. If you extend your stay in the region, our guide to [visiting the châteaux of the Loire](/en/blog/visiting-loire-chateaux) will help your guests make the most of Touraine.

To check our availability and receive a bespoke proposal, visit the [wedding](/en/chateau-wedding-loire) page or write to us. We reply within 24 hours.
